{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>From lack of everything, and you shall serve your enemies in want of everything.</b> This is among the attributes of the Holy One, blessed be He — measure for measure. They did not serve the Holy One, blessed be He, from abundance of everything; therefore they shall serve their enemies in want of everything. From this the Rabbis of blessed memory derived in the first chapter of Ḥagigah, citing (Isaiah 48:10) ״הנה צרפתיך ולא בכסף בחרתיך כור עוני״ — 'Behold I have refined you, but not as silver; I have chosen you in the furnace of affliction' — which teaches that the Holy One, blessed be He, searched through all good measures and found no remedy for Israel other than poverty. Shmuel said: this is what people say — poverty befits Israel like a red saddle-strap on a white horse."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:43.422223576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}